    {
        "content": "<p>Just wondering:<br>\nhas anyone ever explored whether you can prevent users from passing Options to your API?</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Rust\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"k\">pub</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">trait</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Foo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">fn</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">borrow_back</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"o\">&amp;</span><span class=\"k\">mut</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">data</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nc\">T</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">// &lt;- should borrow back</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"k\">struct</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nc\">Bar</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">data</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nc\">T</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"k\">impl</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Bar</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"k\">pub</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fn</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">new</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">data</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nc\">T</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">-&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nc\">Bar</span><span class=\"o\">&lt;</span><span class=\"n\">T</span><span class=\"o\">&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">// should take ownership of T</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>In <code>borrow_back()</code>, users could just do a data.take(), if it's an option, thereby sort of bypassing your ownership model.</p>\n<p>Not a huge issue for me, but I was wondering if someone has explored preventing that</p>",
        "id": 637885979,
        "sender_full_name": "Philipp Stanner",
        "timestamp": 1793898146
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I would assume you mean <code>borrow_back(data: &amp;mut T)</code>, right? Not sure the other one compiles.</p>",
        "id": 638052712,
        "sender_full_name": "Andreas Hindborg",
        "timestamp": 1793952098
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>When you provide a mutable reference as a function parameter, the function will be allowed to move out of the thing the reference points to (place?). If you don't want that, you put the reference behind a <code>Pin</code>.</p>",
        "id": 638053011,
        "sender_full_name": "Andreas Hindborg",
        "timestamp": 1793952183
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Of course your <code>T</code> must be <code>!Unpin</code> for this to work.</p>",
        "id": 638053080,
        "sender_full_name": "Andreas Hindborg",
        "timestamp": 1793952204
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>As far as I understand, a new <code>Move</code> trait is in the works that would replace the <code>Pin</code> stuff. I think it is <a href=\"https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/issues/149607\">this one</a>. I am not sure of the roadap.</p>",
        "id": 638053601,
        "sender_full_name": "Andreas Hindborg",
        "timestamp": 1793952363
    }
]